    <dcterms:title>Barry Lyndon</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Luck_of_Barry_Lyndon</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by Steve Harris, Charles Franks, David Widger and the Online
Distributed Proofreading Team</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"Barry Lyndon" by William Makepeace Thackeray is a picaresque novel first published in 1844. An Irish gentleman schemes his way toward English aristocracy through a life of duels, military service, gambling, and seduction. Narrated by the unreliable Barry himself, the story follows his relentless pursuit of wealth and status across war-torn Europe. From fraudulent courtships to strategic marriages, Barry's fortunes rise and fall as ambition collides with fate, leading to a reckoning that strips away his carefully constructed identity. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 68.2 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
